course: dictionary
lesson: 8349
title: Finding the root of a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Root has more than one meaning, so check the context to find the right one. «The tree's roots spread far under the path.» Here a root is the part of a plant that grows under the ground. «The root of the problem was a broken pipe.» Here root means the cause of something.
explain: Roots can also mean where a person's family comes from. If someone says their roots are in Kenya, they mean their family started there. In a sentence, ask yourself which meaning fits best, then try it out.
explain: Words are built from roots. The root is the main part, and you can add a prefix to the start and a suffix to the end. «Un» + «happy» + «ness» makes «unhappiness». Once you spot the root, the rest of the word is easier to understand.
fact: A root is the part of a plant under the ground that holds it in place and takes in water.
fact: «Roots» can also mean the place where a person's family comes from.
fact: The root word is the main part a longer word is built from, like «happy» in «unhappiness».
fact: In maths, the square root of 9 is 3, because 3 × 3 = 9.
fact: «Mangrove roots break the waves and hold the soil, like a sponge and a fence in one.»
exercise: «The plant's root grows under the ground.» What is a root? | A seed that falls off in autumn | The flower on top of the stem | The green leaves that catch the sun | *The part of a plant under the ground that holds it in place
exercise: In «happy», «unhappy» and «happiness», what is the root word? | happiness | *happy | unhappy | ness
exercise: Nadia says, «Let's root for our team!» What does root for mean here? | To hide from them | To count the goals | To dig up the ground | *To cheer for them
test: What is the square root of 16? | 12 | 6 | *4 | 8
test: «The root of the problem was a broken pipe.» What does root mean here? | A part of a plant | A hair on your head | A search for treasure | *The cause of something
exam: «Mangrove roots break the waves and hold the soil.» What do the roots do? | Sing to the young fish | Grow fruit for the fish | *Break the waves and hold the soil | Make the sea salty
